          "checks": "Actions and improvised GM rolls; Attack one melee/ranged with Extra Attack exception; cast time not always an action; Dash uses modified speed; Disengage remainder of TURN; Dodge requires seeing attacker and lost on incapacitation/speed0; Help next check or first allied attack at5feet before next turn; Hide/Search/UseObject read. Ready perceivable trigger, reaction AFTER trigger finishes, optional ignore, act before next turn; readied spell requires1action cast and concentration, and loss dissipates without effect. Source says one reaction per round in Ready; more precise reset rule is earlier Reactions. Translation retains source sentence, no new round-based engine rule introduced."
